type="local"
addr="hejohns">Johnson He</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:parent>hejohns-0006</fr:parent></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><fr:p>
        Notice that <fr:link
href="sub-0006.xml"
type="local"
addr="sub-0006">the above proof</fr:link> does <fr:em>not</fr:em> use the information that <fr:tex>u</fr:tex> is monotone.
        Thus <fr:link
href="hejohns-0006.xml"
type="local"
addr="hejohns-0006">the above lemma</fr:link> holds where <fr:tex>f</fr:tex> and <fr:tex>u</fr:tex> are just a priori functions.
        The <fr:link
href="hejohns-0006.xml"
type="local"
addr="hejohns-0006">above lemma</fr:link> is in some sense the more
        immediately natural question, but can be easily strengthened to
        the form of this corollary.
    </fr:p></fr:mainmatter><fr:backmatter><fr:contributions></fr:contributions><fr:context><fr:tree
