        (For <fr:tex>V</fr:tex>-enriched categories, ) If <fr:tex>V</fr:tex> is thin, all diagrams commute,
        thus an adjunction core always determines an adjunction.
    </fr:p><fr:p><fr:tex>Set</fr:tex> isn't thin, but <fr:tex>2</fr:tex> is, thus for posets, an adjunction core
        gives rise to a thin adjunction, as remarked <fr:link
href="subb-0006.xml"
type="local"
addr="subb-0006">here</fr:link>.
        I don't know how useful this lemma is for ordinary Homset categories.
    </fr:p></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree></fr:backlinks><fr:references></fr:references></fr:backmatter></fr:tree>